Undockerize + Options Parsing Refactor Plan

Goals
- Fix and unify option parsing across all commands so both short flags (-c) and long flags (--cn and --cn=value) always work consistently.
- Undockerize defaults: make Simple CA runnable without Docker by defaulting to XDG paths (e.g., ~/.local/state/simple-ca) while preserving Docker support via env vars.

Conventions to implement
- Parsing: Use portable manual while/case argument parsing (POSIX-compatible) per repo rules; support:
  - Short flags: -f -k value -r value
  - Long flags: --force, --key-type value, --key-type=value
  - Stop parsing on --
  - -h/--help prints usage to stdout and exits 0; errors print to stderr and exit non-zero
  - Consistent error messages: "Unknown option: --xyz" and "Missing argument for --key-type"
- XDG paths:
  - basePath default: ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/simple-ca
  - exportDir default: ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/simple-ca/export
  - rootConfig, intermediateConfig default to ${SCRIPT_DIR}/openssl-*.cnf
  - Still honor env overrides if provided (basePath, exportDir, rootConfig, intermediateConfig)
  - Add global CLI options to override paths: --base-path, --export-dir
- Maintain Docker compatibility by setting ENV in Dockerfile so container keeps /opt paths by default.

Task 1 — Normalize option parsing across all subcommands
- Files:
  - src/init.sh
  - src/request-server-cert.sh
  - src/validate.sh
  - src/eject-ca.sh
  - src/re-init.sh
  - src/cert-manager.sh (already close; align behavior and messages)
- Edits:
  - Replace getopts-only flows with a manual while [[ $# -gt 0 ]] parser supporting both short and long options (with and without =).
  - Ensure both "--opt value" and "--opt=value" are accepted for options requiring a value.
  - Ensure -h|--help handled uniformly and exits 0 after printing usage.
  - Standardize error messages and exit codes (2 for usage errors).
  - Keep positional arguments behavior intact (e.g., re-init [archive], issue [hostname]).
- Acceptance criteria:
  - For each script, the following invocations behave identically:
    - short: -c value, -o value, -p value
    - long with equals: --cn=value, --output=file.tar.gz, --pass-file=path
    - long with space: --cn value, --output file.tar.gz, --pass-file path
  - Unknown options error with clear message and non-zero exit.
  - Missing value errors are detected for all value-taking options.

Task 2 — Add unit tests for option parsing correctness
- New tests:
  - tests/unit/options_init.bats
  - tests/unit/options_issue.bats
  - tests/unit/options_validate.bats
  - tests/unit/options_eject.bats
  - tests/unit/options_reinit.bats
  - tests/unit/options_cert_manager.bats
- Coverage:
  - Validate short and long variants (with = and with space).
  - Validate unknown option handling.
  - Validate missing value errors.
  - Validate positional argument handling where applicable.
- Acceptance criteria:
  - make test-unit passes and exercises both long and short paths for each command.

Task 3 — Introduce XDG defaults and global path flags
- Files:
  - src/common.sh (defaults)
  - src/main.sh (global flag parsing)
- Edits in src/common.sh:
  - Compute default_xdg_state_dir="${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}".
  - Default basePath to "${default_xdg_state_dir}/simple-ca" when basePath not set.
  - Default exportDir to "${default_xdg_state_dir}/simple-ca/export" when exportDir not set.
  - Default rootConfig and intermediateConfig to "${SCRIPT_DIR}/openssl-*.cnf" when not set.
  - Ensure directories are created as needed (mkdir -p on use sites, not at import time) with restrictive permissions.
- Edits in src/main.sh:
  - Add global flags: --base-path <dir>, --export-dir <dir> (and optional short forms -B, -E if we want).
  - After parsing, export basePath/exportDir so subcommands inherit.
  - Update help text to mention XDG defaults and new global flags.
- Acceptance criteria:
  - Running scripts without any env produces CA under ~/.local/state/simple-ca by default.
  - Global flags override defaults for all subcommands (e.g., simpleca --base-path /tmp/ca init).

Task 4 — Remove hard-coded /opt paths and make config writing unconditional
- Files:
  - src/request-server-cert.sh
  - src/init.sh
  - src/cert-manager.sh
  - src/eject-ca.sh, src/re-init.sh (exportDir usage)
- Edits:
  - Stop checking for basePath == "/opt/ca" to decide whether to generate per-run openssl config; always generate configs using rootCAPath/intermediatePath.
  - Replace any remaining /opt/export assumptions with exportDir.
  - Ensure copy/permissions in issue/eject/validate respect exportDir and do not assume /opt.
- Acceptance criteria:
  - No /opt/ references remain in code paths except Dockerfile ENV and comments.
  - issue/eject/validate work with XDG defaults and with custom --base-path/--export-dir.

Task 5 — Preserve Docker compatibility
- Files:
  - Dockerfile
  - Readme.md
- Edits:
  - Dockerfile: set ENV basePath=/opt/ca exportDir=/opt/export rootConfig=/opt/tools/openssl-root.cnf intermediateConfig=/opt/tools/openssl-intermediate.cnf to keep existing container paths without code changes.
  - Keep ENTRYPOINT ./main.sh.
- Acceptance criteria:
  - make docker-test still passes.
  - Container behavior unchanged relative to current usage.

Task 6 — Developer UX: runnable without Docker and simple wrapper
- Files:
  - create new: bin/simpleca (small shim to exec src/main.sh)
  - Makefile (optional install)
  - Readme.md
- Edits:
  - Add a lightweight wrapper script bin/simpleca that execs src/main.sh so PATH usage is easy (or instruct running src/main.sh directly).
  - Add Makefile target install (optional) to copy bin/simpleca to /usr/local/bin.
  - Document host usage and XDG defaults in Readme.md, including how to override paths and how to migrate from Docker volume.
- Acceptance criteria:
  - Running simpleca on host with no env works and writes to ~/.local/state/simple-ca.

Task 7 — Optional: migration helper (nice-to-have)
- New subcommand: simpleca migrate
  - Detect legacy /opt/ca (or a provided --from) and migrate to XDG default or --to path.
  - Safety checks: refuse to overwrite unless --force.
- Acceptance criteria:
  - simpleca migrate copies (or moves) CA directories and updates permissions.
  - Not required for initial completion; tracked as follow-up.

Task 8 — Tests and quality gates
- Run and fix:
  - make lint
  - make test (unit, integration, e2e)
  - make docker-test
- Add new unit tests for main global flags --base-path/--export-dir and XDG defaults.
- Ensure shellcheck passes on all new/modified scripts.

Concrete edit checklist per file
- src/common.sh
  - Change defaults to XDG; default configs to ${SCRIPT_DIR}/openssl-*.cnf.
- src/main.sh
  - Add --base-path, --export-dir; mention in usage; export after parse.
- src/init.sh
  - Manual parsing with both short/long variants; no getopts; help text unchanged; no /opt assumptions.
- src/request-server-cert.sh
  - Manual parsing; accept --pass-file with and without =; always generate per-run configs using paths; remove /opt special casing; keep behavior of SERVER_CN positional fallback.
- src/validate.sh
  - Manual parsing; accept --pass-file with and without =.
- src/eject-ca.sh
  - Manual parsing; accept --output with and without =; write to exportDir.
- src/re-init.sh
  - Manual parsing; positional archive respected; if relative, resolve under exportDir.
- src/cert-manager.sh
  - Align errors/messages; ensure both forms are accepted for all options; default OUT_DIR to ${exportDir}/manifests.
- Dockerfile
  - Add ENV basePath/exportDir/config paths to preserve container defaults.
- Readme.md
  - Document XDG defaults, new flags, and host vs Docker usage.
- tests/*
  - Add unit tests listed above; ensure existing integration/e2e remain green.

Verification steps
- Host (no Docker):
  - rm -rf ~/.local/state/simple-ca
  - ./src/main.sh init (or bin/simpleca init)
  - ./src/main.sh issue --cn test.local --sans DNS:test.local
  - Confirm files under ~/.local/state/simple-ca
- Container:
  - make docker-test
  - docker run --rm -e basePath=/opt/ca -e exportDir=/opt/export simpleca:latest version

Out-of-scope but noted
- Consider permissions of exported files (avoid chmod 776; prefer 644/600) — can be addressed in a later hardening pass.
- Consider adding a config file under XDG_CONFIG_HOME for defaults.
